.ram
# The RAM disk the tpm and rescue families work on: secrets, auth hashes,
# session contexts and the rescue passphrase never touch a disk. Relative
# to the database (.ram) or absolute. 'elebake ram open' mounts a tmpfs of
# 64 MiB there, owned by the database's owner; 'elebake ram close' wipes
# and unmounts it. stage rescue passphrase opens it itself.
